The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS': {'HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS': ['_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_OPTIMIZED_SCHEMA_VARIANTS_20150220', '_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_VARIANTS_20150220', '_1000_GENOMES_SAMPLE_INFO', 'PLATINUM_GENOMES_DEEPVARIANT_VARIANTS_20180823', 'SIMONS_GENOME_DIVERSITY_PROJECT_SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES', 'SIMONS_GENOME_DIVERSITY_PROJECT_SAMPLE_METADATA', 'SIMONS_GENOME_DIVERSITY_PROJECT_SAMPLE_VARIANTS', '_1000_GENOMES_PEDIGREE']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant table & column mapping  
• reference_bases : filter on the two reference‑allele strings “AT” and “TA”.  
• start_position : numerical coordinate used to derive the minimum / maximum.  
• partition_date_please_ignore : restrict rows to the Phase‑3 snapshot “2015‑02‑20”.  
• (optional) reference_name, end_position, AN, NS … may help for extra context or
  denominator counts if you want “proportions”.

Typical WHERE‑clause pieces  
• "partition_date_please_ignore" = '2015‑02‑20'  
• "reference_bases" IN ('AT','TA')  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows) that
progress from simple inspection to the full min / max / proportion summary you
ultimately need.

```sql
-- 1) Peek at a few rows that have reference_bases = 'AT' or 'TA'
SELECT *
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_OPTIMIZED_SCHEMA_VARIANTS_20150220"
WHERE "partition_date_please_ignore" = '2015-02-20'
  AND "reference_bases" IN ('AT','TA')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct values of reference_bases after filtering, to verify we only get AT / TA
SELECT DISTINCT "reference_bases"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_OPTIMIZED_SCHEMA_VARIANTS_20150220"
WHERE "partition_date_please_ignore" = '2015-02-20'
  AND "reference_bases" IN ('AT','TA')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Simple count of variants by reference_bases
SELECT "reference_bases",
       COUNT(*) AS "var_count"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_OPTIMIZED_SCHEMA_VARIANTS_20150220"
WHERE "partition_date_please_ignore" = '2015-02-20'
  AND "reference_bases" IN ('AT','TA')
GROUP BY "reference_bases"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Minimum start_position for each reference_bases
SELECT "reference_bases",
       MIN("start_position") AS "min_start_pos"
FROM "HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS"."_1000_GENOMES_PHASE_3_OPTIMIZED_SCHEMA_VARIANTS_20150220"
WHERE "partition_date_please_ignore" = '2015-02-20'
  AND "reference_bases" IN ('AT','TA')
GROUP BY "reference_bases"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Maximum start_position for each reference_bases
SELECT "reference_bases",
       MAX("start_position") AS "max_start_pos"
